@node Top
@top News Analysis System Tutorial

The News Analysis System keeps an argument map of a news story.  For
each question a story raises, it tells you whether the evidence public
at a given moment supports an answer, what that answer rests on, and
what new evidence would change it.  This tutorial teaches the ideas from
the ground up, then shows you how to write a case of your own.

Review status: this tutorial was drafted by Claude (Anthropic) at
Andrew Dougherty's direction on 14 October 2026.  Every command output
shown was checked against the running engine.  Andrew has looked it
over but has not yet verified it.

